    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive engine is headlined by **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Gunnar Henderson** (69.47). **Jackson Merrill** represents our highest upside play, benefiting from a soft matchup against Merrill Kelly (5.37 xERA) and an ideal spot at the top of the order. Meanwhile, **Gunnar Henderson** remains a must-start despite the tough platoon split; his 16% park factor boost and elite talent profile neutralize the matchup against David Peterson. **Heliot Ramos** (66.63) and **Coby Mayo** (66.71) are also locked in as strong plays, with **Heliot Ramos** specifically benefiting from a wind-aided environment in a favorable matchup against Ryan Feltner.\n\nThe primary tactical consideration for today\u2019s lineup involves balancing these high-efficiency starts against our bench depth. **Josh Jung** (49.05) was the closest candidate to cracking the active roster, performing admirably in his projection, but he was ultimately edged out by **Miguel Vargas** (52.94) and **Dominic Smith** (56.80), whose specific platoon advantages against Sandoval and Keller, respectively, provided higher projected utility. We are also monitoring several \"Lineup Pending\" designations, most notably for **Liam Hicks** and **Cole Carrigg**; should their confirmed batting positions shift significantly downward, their efficiency scores will require re-evaluation to avoid wasting valuable game caps. \n\nRisk remains concentrated in the matchups against top-tier arms like Bryce Miller. **Liam Hicks** (42.26) faces the steepest climb of our starters against Miller's 2.44 xERA; while his status as a leadoff hitter keeps him in the mix, his floor is thinner than that of **Jacob Wilson** (68.72), who finds himself in a surprisingly favorable spot against Framber Valdez. We are operating with a cautious eye on **Josh Lowe**, whose projection (46.37) is hampered by an unfavorable slot at the bottom of the order against Nathan Eovaldi. Provided the weather holds, the Austin Waves are well-positioned to capitalize on these matchups to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 standings.",
